WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.940
I... I want to help Rein more.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.150
I want to stay with Rein and everyone...

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.680
Sure thing.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.830
But I'm already contracted to all the others,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.010
so I'm not sure 
if I can contract with you, too.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.000
Okay, here I go.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.200
My name is Rein Shroud.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.840
In establishing this new contract, 
a bond is formed.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.780
An oath in our hearts, hopes in our souls...

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.160
Your power, in my hand.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.500
Speak now your name.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.240
Nina.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.510
The contract is sealed.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.470
Yeah!

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.120
We're beast buddies!

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.950
You can call me "big sis" if you want!

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.320
Hold it, Kanade!

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.940
Leave a little cuddling for me!

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.440
I, too, have always desired 
a charming little sister!

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.590
Big Sis!

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.160
Though, I can't say 
I don't feel the same way!

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:57.840
<b>Beast Tamer</b>

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.970
A Home for All

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.970
A Home for All

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.130
Rein!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.480
Stella?

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.840
What's the captain of the Knights 
doing at the adventurers' guild?

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:29.190
We've been discussing 
a collaboration of sorts.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.000
I've been asking for the guild's help 
maintaining order

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.690
while the city's still in chaos.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.400
We'd never have considered it 
under the old Knights' regime,

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.530
but with Captain Stella in charge, 
it's a welcome offer.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.440
Oh? Nicely done, Captain.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.400
Glad to hear you're all getting along!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.990
Things are looking up, then?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.630
They are.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.830
I'm going to make the former 
lord pay all of his debts!

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.130
I feel like I've burdened you 
a little with all this.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:57.800
Nonsense!

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.790
I would never have been able to openly 
work for the city's sake before now.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.630
I simply couldn't be more pleased.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.720
Thank you again, Rein, everyone.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.910
It's truly been my honor to know you.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:09.890
Stella...

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.280
I know!

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.380
Rein, the guild has business 
with your party, as well!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.850
The guild? With us?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.570
Congratulations!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:24.280
You're officially promoted 
to a C-rank adventurer!

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.360
Clap, clap, clap, clap!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.110
Um, Miss Natalie?

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.420
I only became E-rank.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.040
And why C instead of D?

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:36.970
You exposed the wrongdoings 
of the lord's son,

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:41.070
and performed the incredible feat of 
vanquishing an A-rank-equivalent demon!

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.870
That deserves far more than a single rank-up!

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:45.760
We made a special exception.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.900
You can hold your head high.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.140
This wasn't just the guild's decision.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.350
Stella and the other 
adventurers asked for it, too.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.190
I was just trying to protect the city.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.410
And I couldn't have done it 
without my party's help...

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.690
Just accept the honor!

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.160
Rein is always far too humble.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:03.780
Yeah!

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.170
Rein's amazing!

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.280
Yeah!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.490
Everyone's recognizing how strong you are!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.720
Recognizing... me?

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.770
You can expect significant 
compensation, as well.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:18.710
<i>Very</i> significant!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.180
Okay, then we'll have a feast!

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.860
Pick anything you like!

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.660
Fish!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:24.250
Meat!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.310
Hot dogs!

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.200
Fried tofu...

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.680
Can we have multiple helpings?

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.030
And if I might ask...

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.470
As many as you like!

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.220
Have you added a newcomer?

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.880
Yeah, sorry for not introducing her sooner.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.880
This is my new comrade, Nina.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.980
I-I'm Nina...

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.480
So cute!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.730
But wait a minute...

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.940
Is she a demigod?!

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.700
Another ultimate species?

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.910
Yeah, why?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:52.370
Um... do you think she's angry 
that I treated her as a child?

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.330
I'm not angry.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.200
So cute!

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.450
Wait, Miss Natalie!

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.650
Don't hog her!

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.190
I wish to cuddle her, as well!

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.040
The tails are ours!

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.330
Nina's sort of the reason we came here today.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.470
Me?

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.460
Our room's way too small 
for a six-member party.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:17.310
I was wondering if the guild had any advice.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.520
I see...

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.820
Would you consider buying a house, then?

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:22.700
A house?

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.160
Many parties buy a house 
to serve as a home base.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.780
The guild actually serves as property agents 
and provides subsidies, as well.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:35.490
Particularly for talented adventurers 
we'd like to lock down locally!

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.470
Her eyes are so predatory!

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.080
Feels like she wants to trap us in the city!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.820
A house, huh?

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:43.540
What do you all think?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.790
Sounds great to me!

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:49.580
I like this city, and sharing 
a house with Rein sounds fun!

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.610
It does sound more inviting than the inn.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.700
Th-The "staying with Rein" part 
is immaterial, of course.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:57.530
Having a home base would be very convenient!

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.940
Just make sure it's worthy of my greatness!

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:05.450
We do have quite a hefty savings, 
and if the guild will chip in, too...

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.240
All right! Let's buy a house!

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.990
Yeah!

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:25.350
Nothing we've seen seems right.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.010
Here's the final property I have to show you!

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:35.840
It's a wooden house with a large lawn, 
as Kanade and Sora wanted.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:39.790
It has over ten rooms, 
with large beds, as Tania requested.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:43.730
And it has the kitchen and big bath 
that Runa and Nina asked for!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.940
It also comes furnished 
and it's within your budget!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.900
Well? What do you think?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.090
Hold on.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:53.500
If the property's that great, 
why wasn't it the first one you showed us?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.390
That's a very good question!

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:58.080
I smell manipulation!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.460
<i>Stare...</i>

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:10.050
The house is... haunted.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.640
Haunted? You mean by ghosts—

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.010
K-Kanade?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.760
I can't s-stand ghosts!

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.200
You're pathetic.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:23.050
What kind of ultimate species 
is afraid of a few ghosts?

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:25.120
Everyone's got things they're scared of!

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:28.590
Physical attacks don't work on them, 
and they can possess you!

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:29.960
There, there.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:34.400
Might I ask what it is 
the ghosts <i>do</i>, precisely?

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:35.860
Well...

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.790
They turn over your pillow 
right before you lie down.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:44.000
They turn your bathwater cold.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.210
They swap your sugar 
and salt while you're eating.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.670
They stick rotten eggs in your shoes.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:55.290
They smear leftover curry 
on your drying laundry!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:59.480
These awful paranormal incidents 
have left us without buyers.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:01.310
No!

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.800
It all seems mild...

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.060
But it does make it rather unwelcoming.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.100
But it's too nice a house 
to just give up on, right?

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.520
I agree, but...

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:15.130
I c-can probably handle it... 
if you're a-all with me...

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.120
I w-won't be scared of ghosts...

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.260
Here's what we'll do.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.710
We'll check out the house 
and see what we can do about it.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:26.490
A fine idea.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.540
I'm in!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.500
I'll wait here and secure your escape route!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.200
Take care, now!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.080
<i>Oh, she's not coming?</i>

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.930
Well, let's go!

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.640
Yeah!

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.640
Yeah...

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.640
Y-Yeah...

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.610
Would you mind watching 
where you put your hands?

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.320
C-Can't help it...

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:04.830
Ow!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.100
Rather tidy for a haunted house, isn't it?

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:09.870
Yes.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:13.240
It almost appears 
to receive regular cleanings.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.070
What was that?

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:17.210
W-We didn't do anything!

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.090
Is this what they call a poltergeist?

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.550
Get out...

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:23.720
Get out...

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.930
The ghost! The ghost is here!

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.600
Calm down! We're all here with you!

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.060
Get out...

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:38.570
Get out!

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.280
Leave this to us!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:45.260
One blast of destruction magic'll 
make short work of that thing!

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.490
We'll use purification magic!

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:47.370
Let us begin!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.000
Holy Circle!

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:54.550
Did it work?

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.790
Get out.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.560
It's still alive!

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.180
It's not technically alive at all, you know.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:06.110
It moved to the astral side 
just before impact, I believe.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.810
That's a pretty smart escape strategy!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.160
Though there are spells 
that'll hit her just as well there...

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.370
But they would likely demolish 
the house along with the spirit.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:16.400
Shall we try it?

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.040
Could you find another way?

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.610
Get out already!

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.060
Careful, everyone!

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.070
Get out, get out!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.280
Get out, get out!

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.940
Get out! Get out!

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:30.680
A thought occurs.

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:33.580
Does that spirit lack any means of attack?

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:33.920
Erk!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.650
I believe that spirit just said "erk."

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.480
Guess the cat's outta the bag.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.800
There, there.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:44.340
Get out!

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.390
Get out!

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.350
Get out!

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.060
Get out!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.940
Get out already! Get out!

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.060
I'm not afraid...

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.520
I'm not afraid...

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.200
M-My clothing!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.410
She harmed the ghost with a physical attack?

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:11.150
Kanade's fear reached its limit and 
allowed the body to transcend the spirit!

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:11.750
Or something like!

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.910
Please, spare me!

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.680
Sacred Seal!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.250
We used a barrier to sever 
her astral side escape route.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.350
No more runnin' for you!

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:39.360
Nothing to be afraid of now, dear.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.940
Huh? What was I doing just now?

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.450
Thank goodness!

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:46.910
Are you ready to talk now?

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.620
You don't seem to be 
a bad person... er, spirit.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:54.040
Time to pull out all the stops...

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.680
I'm takin' that body!

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.460
Stop!

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.250
What's goin' on?

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:01.460
I c-can't move...

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.820
It's because I'm a beast tamer.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.430
Eh? What's that got to do with it?

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:13.850
When I was little, a neighborhood man 
told me about phantom taming.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.690
An' then what?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.650
Eh? That's the whole story.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:21.840
That don't explain 
how you can control us ghosts!

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.110
We hear you.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:29.210
Well, maybe it's the fact that you've got 
a more intact personality than most ghosts,

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:31.980
so maybe my words had more impact?

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:33.560
How should I know?

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:39.560
I ain't gonna be tamed 
by a whippersnapper like you!

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.290
Hold still!

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:48.440
Fine, I give up.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.260
Go on an' burn me up or boil me.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.280
I'm Rein Shroud.

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:54.850
Who are you?

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.400
As I said, I just want to talk.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.360
What a weirdo!

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:07.530
I'm Tina Holy.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.980
I was a maid in another city,

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.280
but I kinda died, 
round about thirty years ago,

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.700
and ended up here.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.500
Then you weren't here the whole time?

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.800
Ain't like I'm bound to a single location.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.650
I can move around pretty well.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:24.220
And how, precisely, did you end up a ghost?

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:25.050
Hold it, Tania!

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:31.890
The guy who ran the mansion I worked 
at was a real sadist pervo womanizer.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.110
He even killed me!

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:36.390
Next thing I knew, I was a ghost.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.050
Don't go askin' me to explain why!

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.150
What do you plan to do next, Tina?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.070
There's a good question.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:45.640
Since I can't drive you out, 
I guess I better go myself.

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.150
Sorry about all the scares.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:50.870
Kanade, are you still scared of Tina?

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.120
Well...

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.710
I am.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:57.830
But if you're all with me, 
we could maybe get along.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.420
Thanks, Kanade.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:12.590
All right, Tina.

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:16.310
Would you like to live here with us?

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.590
Eh? What're you sayin' that for?

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:20.140
I just said I'd clear out...

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:24.890
Actually, having you here 
really knocked down the price.

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.560
So you'd be a big help if you stayed!

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:28.940
Y-You think?

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.040
W-Well, if you insist...

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.940
Hang on, you're just makin' excuses!

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:34.920
That's the kind of person Rein is.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:37.280
You should accept his kindness.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.850
But... you really sure you want me around?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:43.670
A ghost or two isn't a big deal 
to Rein at this point...

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:47.380
Just don't scare me by passing through 
too many walls, okay?

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:50.480
Does being a maid make you a capable cook?

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.570
I would love to take lessons from you!

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.140
We'd love to have ya!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.970
You can skip teachin' Sis 
how to cook, though!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.480
I'm not playing here.

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.180
I mean it, okay?!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.140
N-Nice to meet you.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.800
You mean...

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.860
I look forward to living with you, Tina.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:11.080
S-Same to you!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.790
The contract is officially established.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:22.410
That house officially belongs to you now!

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:24.320
Although...

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:26.940
You truly are exceptional.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.260
You even integrated a ghost into your party!

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:30.320
Her name's Tina!

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:35.060
Right now, we're all working 
on a housewarming party!

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.270
We should go do our part, too, Kanade.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.600
Yeah, they asked us to do the shopping!

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:43.760
I hope we can count 
on you further in the future.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:47.190
Horizon is your home, after all!

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:49.110
Home?

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:54.280
Yeah... we look forward to sticking around!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.050
Here you go.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:00.220
Thank you!

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.300
Might I have a moment, shopkeep?

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:03.460
Feel free—

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.920
The Hero?

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.420
I'll take a week's worth of rations.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:14.630
And I'm afraid I'm short of funds, 
so it'll have to be free.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:17.480
But you'll be helping the Hero's party,

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:19.120
so I'm sure you'd be honored.

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:22.460
To aid the Hero is a duty given by God.

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:23.920
We welcome your assistance.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:26.480
We don't have much choice, after all.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:28.760
I'm terribly sorry,

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:31.940
but I don't have any merchandise 
to spare for you.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.650
Do you realize what you just said?

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:42.400
The Hero's party is on a journey to defeat 
the Demon King and save the world!

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.460
Hero's party, my eye!

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:46.870
You didn't even do anything to save Horizon!

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.430
I beg your pardon.

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:52.480
You think a mere shopkeep

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.980
has the wherewithal to criticize 
the Hero's lofty decision-making?

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:58.410
We don't need this rotten shop.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.920
Arios, let's take our business else—

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:04.140
Don't waste your time! There's not 
a shop here that will gift you provisions!

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.500
How dare you—

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:09.580
Pretty high and mighty for a guy 
who hid out of fear of a demon.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.980
As if they could ever 
beat the Demon King!

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.690
They always seemed off to me.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.130
Get off your high horse!

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:14.070
Learn a little humility!

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.040
Let's go.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:26.820
But Arios, our provisions—

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:29.320
We're never coming back to this lousy town!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.290
That beast tamer's 
more of a Hero than you'll ever be!

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.490
<i>Rein Shroud!</i>

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:40.010
<i>I <i>will</i> be the end of you!</i>

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:46.000
They gave us so much!

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.060
It was a little awkward, but I appreciate it.

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:51.880
It did seem a little noisy 
in the market, didn't it?

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:54.270
I'm sure everyone's just happy to be back!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.730
Really? Glad to hear it.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:58.700
Oh, I know!

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:00.160
Kanade?

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.010
Welcome home!

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.000
<i>Yes, that's right...</i>

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.060
I'm home!

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.100
Tina and Runa made all this?

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.530
Sure did!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.850
As a ghost, I can't really taste-test it,

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.000
but I made it how the recipe says, 
so it oughta be fine.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.310
Awesome! Awesome!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.210
All thanks to my help!

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.150
I never knew you could cook.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.350
Yep!

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:41.240
There wasn't anyone in my home forest 
better at cuttin' up veggies than me!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:44.660
That's why it's me and not Sis 
who'll be runnin' the kitchen!

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:46.620
<i>Please</i> let me run the kitchen!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.300
Runa, I'd like to ask you 
what you meant by that exactly...

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.580
There's so much to eat that
 I don't know where to start...

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.160
Meat! The meat's all mine!

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:56.200
Where's the fish?!

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:59.820
You can't grow up big and strong 
without a balanced diet!

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:02.140
I almost never get to eat fish!

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.120
Big and strong...

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:06.490
You should both lay off those gross 
clumps of fat! They're bad for you!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.930
You know, Rein...

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:07.630
What do you mean?!

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:10.780
Runa, I'd still like that explanation...

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.230
Um... well...

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:12.390
Th-Thank you!

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:17.340
I'm really not alone now!

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:25.770
My home, my family, my town...

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.660
On the day I lost them all,

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:32.500
a large hole opened in my heart.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.350
The same was true for all of us.

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.960
Dunno what we'd have done without ya, Rein.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.600
We're in this together!

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.880
You're all so lucky!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.800
What are you saying now?

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.760
Yeah! You're not alone either, remember?

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:48.650
Oh, yeah?

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.720
Guess I'm not!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.840
Now, get sittin' before it gets cold!

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:56.120
That's right! I'm pretty hungry!

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.650
<i>Maybe becoming an independent adventurer</i>

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:03.070
<i>because traveling with 
Arios's party didn't fill that void</i>

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.530
<i>is just a form of escapism.</i>

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:10.310
<i>But meeting them all...</i>

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:24.920
Rein?

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:26.880
What is it, everyone?

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:30.280
Well... Rein, you're...

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:32.850
Oh...

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:36.380
Right, I'm probably so hungry 
it brought tears to my eyes!

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.240
Yeah, yeah! It's sad when you're hungry, huh?

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.610
I'm willing to share 
some of my meat with you.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:44.110
You must try my own home cooking, as well!

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.730
Rein! I'll hold her off, 
so run while you can!

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:48.070
Let's eat together!

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:49.520
Yeah, yeah!

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.120
Eat as much as y'all want!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.510
Okay, then!

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:55.850
Let's eat!

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:01.820
<i>This is the story of the beast tamer 
driven out of the Hero's party</i>

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:08.630
<i>who met an ultimate species cat girl 
and forged a new set of bonds...</i>

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:12.780
<i>or, at least, that's the story's prologue!</i>
